# Project-level environment overview.
#
# Each application loads its OWN .env file, not this one:
#   backend/.env   (copy from backend/.env.example)
#   mobile/.env    (copy from mobile/.env.example)
#
# This root file exists only as a single discoverable entry point documenting
# that both exist. Never put real secrets in any .env.example file — placeholders only.
#
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT_PLAN.md §4 (Secrets Management) for how these are
# provisioned per environment (development / staging / production).

# Backend runtime config -> backend/.env.example
# Mobile runtime config  -> mobile/.env.example
